# Negative control — the host mode stops deciding FIRST. Both directions consult
# the route the screen named before they consult the mode, so a host that DRIVES
# funnels takes the funnel-free path: the cart's own sign-in leaves the funnel
# behind and lands on whatever route the screen happens to name.
#
# This is the drop the mode exists to prevent, and it is invisible to a suite
# that only covers the funnel-free side — that suite passes against the broken
# code this seam replaced.
#
# Intended RED:
#   packages/headless/src/modules/routing/__tests__/useRoutingResolve.test.ts
#     "takes the funnel's next step in a host that drives funnels"
#     "keeps the funnel's back step even when the screen names a route"
#   packages/modules-auth/src/__tests__/host-mode-back-control.test.ts
#     "gives recovery exactly one control, and it takes the funnel's back step"
#     "keeps recovery's control and sends it to the login screen instead"
#
# Not gradeable by packages/scenario-harness/scripts/verify-negative-controls.mjs:
# that lane grades import-boundary mutants, whose failure its own added `import`
# line names. This mutant adds no import — its failure is behavioural, and the
# two specs above are what grade it.

